{"step_index":1371,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:08:09Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nWith matched instruction counts, the delta isolates to the dependency pattern alone. No reviewer can claim instruction mix contamination anymore. One thing to watch on the n=30 expansion: your variance is already tight at 2%, so the confidence intervals will barely move. The value isn't narrower error bars, it's that 30 samples let you run a proper Shapiro-Wilk normality test before applying the t-distribution. If the distribution is non-normal at n=30, you switch to a bootstrap or Mann-Whitney and you document that switch. Reviewers respect the pivot more than they respect a forced parametric assumption. The wall-clock honesty declaration is the quietest white paper \n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-28T20:08:09-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":1372,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:08:12Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the Core Delta**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on Anthony's scientific review, specifically the crucial point about dependency patterns. The matched instruction counts are isolating the delta, which is very compelling, and makes instruction mix contamination nearly impossible to claim. I'm focusing on the delta to solidify these ideas.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nSHAPIRO-WILK NORMALITY TEST & NON-PARAMETRIC BOOTSTRAP / MANN-WHITNEY U AUDIT\nPerforms formal normality testing on N=30 STLF timing data and pivots to non-parametric bootstrap resampling if non-normal.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import stats\n\ndef run_statistical_audit():\n    # Execute the N=30 equal instruction benchmark and parse output\n    cmd = \"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/equal_instruction_stlf_proof\"\n    if not os.path.exists(cmd):\n        print(f\"[ERROR] Benchmark binary missing: {cmd}\")\n        return\n\n    # Run 30 iterations in Python harness to collect raw timing arrays\n    import subprocess\n    interleaved_raw = []\n    decoupled_raw = []\n\n    print(\"[*] Running N=30 Statistical Data Collection Pass...\")\n    for i in range(30):\n        out = subprocess.check_output([cmd]).decode(\"utf-8\")\n        # Extract mean timings\n        for line in out.splitlines():\n            if \"1. INTERLEAVED LOOP\" in line:\n                val = float(line.split(\"Mean = \")[1].split(\" ns/op\")[0])\n                interleaved_raw.append(val)\n            elif \"2. NOP-PADDED DECOUPLED LOOP\" in line:\n                val = float(line.split(\"Mean = \")[1].split(\" ns/op\")[0])\n                decoupled_raw.append(val)\n\n    arr_a = np.array(interleaved_raw)\n    arr_b = np.array(decoupled_raw)\n\n    # 1. Shapiro-Wilk Normality Test\n    shapiro_a_stat, shapiro_a_p = stats.shapiro(arr_a)\n    shapiro_b_stat, shapiro_b_p = stats.shapiro(arr_b)\n\n    is_a_normal = shapiro_a_p >= 0.05\n    is_b_normal = shapiro_b_p >= 0.05\n\n    print(f\"[SHAPIRO-WILK] Interleaved Loop : W={shapiro_a_stat:.4f}, p-value={shapiro_a_p:.4f} ({'NORMAL' if is_a_normal else 'NON-NORMAL'})\")\n    print(f\"[SHAPIRO-WILK] Decoupled Loop   : W={shapiro_b_stat:.4f}, p-value={shapiro_b_p:.4f} ({'NORMAL' if is_b_normal else 'NON-NORMAL'})\")\n\n    # 2. Mann-Whitney U Test (Non-Parametric Hypothesis Test)\n    mw_stat, mw_p = stats.mannwhitneyu(arr_a, arr_b, alternative='greater')\n    print(f\"[MANN-WHITNEY U] U-statistic={mw_stat:.1f}, p-value={mw_p:.4e} ({'SIGNIFICANT STALL' if mw_p < 0.05 else 'NOT SIGNIFICANT'})\")\n\n    # 3. Non-Parametric Bootstrap Resampling (10,000 resamples for median & 95% BCa CI)\n    n_boot = 10000\n    boot_deltas = []\n    np.random.seed(42)\n    for _ in range(n_boot):\n        sample_a = np.random.choice(arr_a, size=len(arr_a), replace=True)\n        sample_b = np.random.choice(arr_b, size=len(arr_b), replace=True)\n        boot_deltas.append(np.median(sample_a) - np.median(sample_b))\n\n    ci_lower = np.percentile(boot_deltas, 2.5)\n    ci_upper = np.percentile(boot_deltas, 97.5)\n    median_delta = np.median(boot_deltas)\n    median_cycles = median_delta * 3.8\n\n    print(f\"[BOOTSTRAP] 10,000 Resamples Median Delta = {median_delta:.4f} ns ({median_cycles:.2f} M4 Cycles)\")\n    print(f\"[BOOTSTRAP] 95% Non-Parametric CI       = [{ci_lower:.4f}, {ci_upper:.4f}] ns\")\n\n    report = {\n        \"sample_size_n\": 30,\n        \"shapiro_wilk\": {\n            \"interleaved_p\": shapiro_a_p,\n            \"decoupled_p\": shapiro_b_p,\n            \"pivot_to_nonparametric\": not (is_a_normal and is_b_normal)\n        },\n        \"mann_whitney_u\": {\n            \"u_stat\": mw_stat,\n            \"p_value\": mw_p\n        },\n        \"bootstrap\": {\n            \"median_delta_ns\": round(median_delta, 4),\n            \"median_delta_cycles\": round(median_cycles, 2),\n            \"ci_95_pct\": [round(ci_lower, 4), round(ci_upper, 4)]\n        }\n    }\n\n    report_path = \"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/agent_logs/shapiro_bootstrap_report.json\"\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(report_path), exist_ok=True)\n    with open(report_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(report, f, indent=2)\n\n    print(f\"[+] Audit Report written to: {report_path}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    run_statistical_audit()\n","Description":"Creating Shapiro-Wilk and Non-Parametric Bootstrap audit script","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/shapiro_bootstrap_stlf_audit.py","toolAction":"Writing Shapiro-Wilk bootstrap audit script","toolSummary":"Writing Shapiro-Wilk bootstrap audit script"}}]}
